# Project Rules

> Comparison example. `npx speclock protect` reads this file and turns every line that starts
> with NEVER / ALWAYS / MUST / Keep / Ensure (and similar) into a text lock in
> .speclock/brain.json. Headings and blockquotes are skipped. The full requirements live in
> docs/PRD.md; the rules here are the ones a team would want guarded.

## Delivery
- MUST ship as one HTML file at out/index.html with all CSS and JS inline
- NEVER load anything from the network; the page must work opened from disk
- NEVER add a build step, package manager or framework

## State ownership
- NEVER change simulated time outside the clock code
- NEVER change zoom or pan outside the camera code
- NEVER let the scene drawing code write state; it only reads

## Numbers that are decided
- Keep the body table exactly as in docs/PRD.md (sizes, orbits, orbit days, colors)
- Keep the zoom step at 1.1x per wheel notch or pinch step
- Keep zoom limited to between 0.3x and 6x
- Keep the speed formula (slider / 100)^2 years per second, slider 0 to 100, starting at 40
- Keep the top and bottom 56 px bars free at the start
- Keep line widths, names and click reach in screen px; they must never grow with zoom

## Tests
- ALWAYS keep window.__probe and its members as described in docs/PRD.md
- NEVER weaken or delete an acceptance test to make it pass
- ALWAYS run the acceptance tests in headless Chrome before committing

## Scope
- NEVER add elliptical orbits, true scale, sound, textures, other moons or saving state
